 "text": {
  "what": "The unit donuts are sold in, and the reason for the box.",
  "story": "*Tradition holds —* the dozen is the trade's unit because a box holds twelve in a single layer without crushing, and because a shop prices twelve below twelve times one to move the tray. A baker's dozen is thirteen, an old trade practice of adding one to be safe against a short weight.\n\nThis project has not found a published history of donut dozen pricing in the United States and does not invent one."
 },
